+*   **When Not to Use:** When interactive exploration or dynamic data adaptation is required [S2].
 
 ## Background
-The concept of hardcoded transfer functions originated in early real-time ray-casting systems like VolumePro, which used pre-computed 4096-entry LUTs loaded into hardware prior to rendering [S2, unofficial]. The implementation details involving CUDA texture objects and device arrays were later popularized in open-source CUDA volume rendering engines [S3, unofficial]. Parametric variants using exponential decay and gradient attenuation have been documented in educational and hobbyist ray-casting tutorials [S4, S6, unofficial].
+The concept of hardcoded transfer functions originated in early real-time ray-casting systems like VolumePro, which used pre-computed 4096-entry LUTs loaded into hardware prior to rendering [S3, unofficial]. CUDA texture object implementations appear in open-source engines [S4, unofficial]. Parametric variants using exponential decay and gradient attenuation have been documented in educational and hobbyist ray-casting tutorials [S5, S7, unofficial].
 
